---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, withBase, yearsShipping } from '../data/site';
import { skillCount } from '../data/skills';
---

<Base title="About" description="Public work on engineering judgment and production AI.">
  <article class="page prose">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-heading">I hold the work to a standard. Then I publish the standard.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I write and teach because production systems punish sloppy thinking, and most AI tools
      make confident mistakes easier. This site is that public practice — {yearsShipping} years of it —
      not a job title.
    </p>
    <p>
      The canonical artifact is{' '}
      <a href={site.ai}>github.com/arunveersingh/ai</a>
      {' '}— {skillCount} agent skills that will say no, not ready, and do not proceed. That is the
      same bar I use on architecture: unverified assumptions do not ship.
    </p>
    <p>
      I teach in English on{' '}
      <a href={site.youtube[0].href}>{site.youtube[0].name}</a>
      {' '}and in Hindi on{' '}
      <a href={site.youtube[1].href}>{site.youtube[1].name}</a>.
      Selected talks on this site are about judgment — first principles, agent pipelines,
      inference, seniority. Syntax drills stay in the library.
    </p>
    <p>
      Writing lives here first, then{' '}
      <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
      Selected systems work:{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/builds/')}>builds</a>
      {' '}— MCP, SBOMs, protocol and architecture labs — not every repo I ever used to learn.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reach me at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. New essays go out over{' '}
      <a href={withBase('rss.xml')}>RSS</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Employment history is LinkedIn. How I think is this site.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
